BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Moon
DTSTART:20250523T180000Z
DTEND:20250523T194500Z
DTSTAMP:20250523T180000Z
UID:X9IwgpZWLt
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 92 mins (1h32m)\n\nAustrian-Kurdish filmmaker Kurdwi
 n Ayub (SIFF 2023’s Sonne) won the Special Jury Prize at the Locarno Fil
 m Festival for her tense\, provocative sophomore feature\, about an MMA fi
 ghter who heads to Jordan to teach a trio of wealthy sisters\, only to lea
 rn they are confined to their home. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/
 festival/moon
LOCATION:AMC Pacific Place 11\, 600 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Shepherds
DTSTART:20250523T193000Z
DTEND:20250523T213500Z
DTSTAMP:20250523T193000Z
UID:koppkLu1Vx
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 113 mins (1h53m)\n\nIn this layered\, bucolic drama 
 from Francophone director Sophie Deraspe (Antigone) full of moments of bea
 uty and harsh reality\, a Quebeçois marketing executive gives it all up a
 nd moves to the French Alps to become a sheep herder. Sponsored by:\n\nhtt
 ps://www.siff.net/festival/shepherds\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • Shoreline 
 CC Theater (Sun 25 May\, 6:00 PM)\n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sanatorium Under the Sign of the Hourglass
DTSTART:20250523T200000Z
DTEND:20250523T213000Z
DTSTAMP:20250523T200000Z
UID:AiPCxm042Y
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 76 mins (1h16m)\n\nThe Brothers Quay spin another fa
 ntastical stop motion yarn with this surreal story inspired by the work of
  Polish writer Bruno Schulz\, about a young man on a ghostly train ride to
 ward a sanatorium that may exist out of time and space. Sponsored by:\n\nh
 ttps://www.siff.net/festival/sanatorium-under-the-sign-of-the-hourglass
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Kingdom
DTSTART:20250523T200000Z
DTEND:20250523T220000Z
DTSTAMP:20250523T200000Z
UID:WGh2ZGWUpG
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 108 mins (1h48m)\n\nWhen an underground war breaks o
 ut between nationalist groups and crime families\, a Corsican mobster and 
 his daughter must go on the run\, bringing them closer together and drawin
 g her into his world. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/the-k
 ingdom
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:To a Land Unknown
DTSTART:20250523T201500Z
DTEND:20250523T221500Z
DTSTAMP:20250523T201500Z
UID:Gg127T33g0
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 106 mins (1h46m)\n\nChatila and Reda are Palestinian
  refugees stuck in Athens\, trying to figure out how to get to Germany\, h
 ow to stay alive in the meanwhile\, and how to do it all without losing th
 eir humanity.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/to-a-land-unknown\n\nAlso p
 laying at:\n  • Shoreline CC Theater (Sat 24 May\, 8:30 PM)
LOCATION:AMC Pacific Place 11\, 600 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Feminine Urge
DTSTART:20250523T203000Z
DTEND:20250523T221500Z
DTSTAMP:20250523T203000Z
UID:U9w8E6K092
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 94 mins (1h34m)\n\nTo spit\, to protest\, to indulge
 \, to break up with a boyfriend…to be a cat.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/fes
 tival/the-feminine-urge\n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beginnings
DTSTART:20250523T220000Z
DTEND:20250523T235000Z
DTSTAMP:20250523T220000Z
UID:xklPtXvlnT
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 96 mins (1h36m)\n\nLife is full of unexpected twists
 . Ane and Thomas (Trine Dyrholm and David Dencik at the top of their craft
 ) must redefine the parameters of their relationship when\, just as they a
 re about to finalize their divorce and tell their two daughters\, she suff
 ers a stroke. Producer Eva Jakobsen and cast Bjørk Storm scheduled to att
 end. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/beginnings
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Paul Anka: His Way
DTSTART:20250523T223000Z
DTEND:20250524T002000Z
DTSTAMP:20250523T223000Z
UID:4qxXvLd0m4
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 99 mins (1h39m)\n\nHe faced it all\, stood tall\, an
 d did it his way. Get the inside scoop on the life and career of Paul Anka
 \, the Canadian-born son of immigrants who rocketed to the top of the char
 ts not just as a teen heartthrob\, but as the songwriter of some of Americ
 a’s greatest standards. Director John Maggio scheduled to attend May 23 
 screening. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/paul-anka-his-wa
 y\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1 (Sun 25 May\, 1:00
  PM)
LOCATION:Shoreline CC Theater\, 16101 Greenwood Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Suburban Fury
DTSTART:20250523T223000Z
DTEND:20250524T004000Z
DTSTAMP:20250523T223000Z
UID:MJTpdPKcuk
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 118 mins (1h58m)\n\nLocal documentarian Robinson Dev
 or (Zoo\, Pow Wow) returns to SIFF with this outré and probing biography 
 of Sara Jane Moore\, the FBI informant and single mother who tried to assa
 ssinate President Gerald Ford in 1975\, as told in her own words. Director
  Robinson Devor\, producer Jason Reid\, executive producer/head archivist 
 Bob Fink\, and co-producer Matt Levinthal scheduled to attend. RSVP to joi
 n Seattle Documentary Association for a happy hour celebrating local docum
 entary filmmaking at Sound Hotel directly before the film. Limited space a
 vailable. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/suburban-fury
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Botanist
DTSTART:20250523T223000Z
DTEND:20250524T002000Z
DTSTAMP:20250523T223000Z
UID:8hQolSMkdi
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 96 mins (1h36m)\n\nIn Jing Yi’s fantastical\, lush
 ly framed drama set in rural northwestern China\, a lonely 13-year-old Kaz
 akh boy in touch with the wonders of nature befriends a local Han girl\, o
 nly for the call of the modern outside world to come calling. Sponsored by
 :\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/the-botanist\n\nAlso playing at:\n  •
  Shoreline CC Theater (Sat 24 May\, 6:00 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Happyend
DTSTART:20250523T224500Z
DTEND:20250524T005000Z
DTSTAMP:20250523T224500Z
UID:WPQL1YrOQv
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 113 mins (1h53m)\n\nIn an earthquake-rattled near-fu
 ture Tokyo\, a multiethnic band of politically aware teens protest their h
 igh school’s draconian and demerit-based new surveillance system in the 
 latest from SIFF alum Neo Sora (2023’s Ryuichi Sakamoto: Opus). Sponsore
 d by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/happyend
LOCATION:AMC Pacific Place 11\, 600 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Adolescent Overdrive
DTSTART:20250523T230000Z
DTEND:20250524T004000Z
DTSTAMP:20250523T230000Z
UID:ssGJTomSRK
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 86 mins (1h26m)\n\nFrom surrealistic swimming lesson
 s to ’90s motocross\, teenage coma musings to rip-roarin’ rodeos\, thi
 s is growing up.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/adolescent-overdrive\n\n
 Film is also being streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Salsa Lives
DTSTART:20250524T004500Z
DTEND:20250524T024000Z
DTSTAMP:20250524T004500Z
UID:gMD543v2xd
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 101 mins (1h41m)\n\nThe rhythms\, passion\, and ener
 gy of Salsa do not recognize borders. Born in the vibrant streets of New Y
 ork\, it conquered and reigned in Cali. Featuring Salsa legends like Rub
 én Blades and Henry Fiol\, this illuminating journey shows how entire ge
 nerations have celebrated their common identity through music and dance. L
 overs of Latin music of a variety of genres will want to attend the May 23
  screening for a chance to win a pair of tickets to the Edmonds Center for
  the Arts' "Selena Experience." And if you live for salsa\, shimmy on down
  to the May 24 screening for some live salsa dancing and instruction by Cl
 ub Sur in the 30 minutes before the film starts. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps:/
 /www.siff.net/festival/salsa-lives\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • Shoreline CC
  Theater (Sat 24 May\, 12:30 PM)\n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:John Cranko
DTSTART:20250524T010000Z
DTEND:20250524T032500Z
DTSTAMP:20250524T010000Z
UID:5v5djSJeiM
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 135 mins (2h15m)\n\nSam Riley (Control) stuns in thi
 s biopic about South African dancer and choreographer John Cranko\, who ov
 ercame self-destructive habits and homophobic persecution as he whipped th
 e 1960s Stuttgart Ballet into an internationally renowned dance company. J
 oin Seattle Speaks German for an informal meetup at Cloudburst Brewing bef
 ore the May 23 screening! At 5:00pm\, the conversation starts in German\, 
 and at 5:45pm\, we’ll walk to the theater together. Open to all! If you 
 love queer cinema\, you'll love the chance to win tickets to the Queer & T
 rans Film Festival\, also at the May 23 screening. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps:
 //www.siff.net/festival/john-cranko\n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Know Her Name
DTSTART:20250524T010000Z
DTEND:20250524T023000Z
DTSTAMP:20250524T010000Z
UID:pHZhDTtGg4
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 80 mins (1h20m)\n\nIn this amazing slice of film her
 story\, learn the legacy of women directors who have fought to be seen and
  heard and have their films preserved…and how to not let the next genera
 tion get lost in the same inequitable and homogenized system. Producer He
 idi Lasi scheduled to attend. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festi
 val/know-her-name\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3 (S
 un 25 May\, 5:00 PM)\n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:Shoreline CC Theater\, 16101 Greenwood Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Flamingos: Life After the Meteorite
DTSTART:20250524T013000Z
DTEND:20250524T030500Z
DTSTAMP:20250524T013000Z
UID:X3JabZgEIQ
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 83 mins (1h23m)\n\nFinding the right partner\, the r
 ight place\, and the ideal time to create a family is the most decisive ta
 sk in nature. Instinct\, love\, and risk are intertwined in this unforgett
 able journey of the Caribbean flamingo in its most delicate period of exis
 tence\; a journey at once surprising\, enthralling\, and deeply inspiring.
  Director Lorenzo Hagerman and producer Jose Cohen scheduled to attend. A 
 few lucky animal lovers will win zoo passes at the May 23 screening\, cour
 tesy of Woodland Park Zoo. Then\, before the May 24 screening\, stop by th
 e Birds Connect Seattle table to learn about their conservation work\, pic
 k up advocacy materials\, and get a rare close-up look at real bird skin s
 pecimens. Expert volunteers will be waiting to chat all things birds with 
 you! Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/flamingos-life-after-t
 he-meteorite\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • Shoreline CC Theater (Sat 24 May\,
  3:30 PM)\n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:AMC Pacific Place 11\, 600 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Time Travel Is Dangerous
DTSTART:20250524T013000Z
DTEND:20250524T032000Z
DTSTAMP:20250524T013000Z
UID:ewnbcbjVbT
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 99 mins (1h39m)\n\nWhat would you do if a time-trave
 l bumper car fell into your lap? If you’re Ruth and Megan of North Londo
 n\, you use it to find and sell antiques at your vintage shop\, of course\
 , regardless of the consequences reverberating across time and space. Dire
 ctor Chris Reading and co-writers/producers Hillary and Anna-Elizabeth Sh
 akespeare scheduled to attend. Satiate your love for sci-fi with tickets t
 o MoPOP\, our trivia giveaway at the May 23 screening.\n\nhttps://www.siff
 .net/festival/time-travel-is-dangerous\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cin
 ema Uptown House 2 (Sat 24 May\, 12:00 PM)\n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Crowd
DTSTART:20250524T020000Z
DTEND:20250524T032000Z
DTSTAMP:20250524T020000Z
UID:VdL8BLn0k2
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 70 mins (1h10m)\n\nA story of a group of friends com
 ing together to plan a farewell party\, The Crowd is also a vibrant portra
 it of a younger generation in Iran\, determined to live life on their own 
 terms. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/the-crowd\n\nAlso pl
 aying at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3 (Sun 25 May\, 12:00 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Everybody Loves Touda
DTSTART:20250524T033000Z
DTEND:20250524T052500Z
DTSTAMP:20250524T033000Z
UID:IPfoQMtZOr
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 101 mins (1h41m)\n\nTouda dreams of being a sheikha\
 , or traditional Moroccan folk singer. But in a culture where female perfo
 rmers are as often eroticized and stigmatized as venerated\, what does it 
 really mean to be loved? Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/ev
 erybody-loves-touda
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:I Am Nevenka
DTSTART:20250524T033000Z
DTEND:20250524T053500Z
DTSTAMP:20250524T033000Z
UID:0GsFQrnO48
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 112 mins (1h52m)\n\nNevenka Fernández\, the town’
 s finance councilor\, is relentlessly pursued by the mayor\, a man used to
  always getting what he wants politically and personally. Nevenka decides 
 to report him\, turning her courageous fight into Spain’s first #MeToo c
 ase. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/i-am-nevenka
LOCATION:Shoreline CC Theater\, 16101 Greenwood Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Raptures
DTSTART:20250524T040000Z
DTEND:20250524T060000Z
DTSTAMP:20250524T040000Z
UID:vaqicKUOkJ
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 108 mins (1h48m)\n\nIn the first-ever film using the
  Indigenous language Meänkieli\, a devout Christian woman in the 1930s li
 ving along the Finland-Sweden border must protect her family from the encr
 oaching wrath of her husband’s newly formed sectarian cult. Join Swedish
  Club NW\, SWEA Seattle\, and fellow lovers of Nordic cinema at the Swedis
 h Club for a 6:00pm happy hour ahead of the May 23 screening. Director Jon
  Blåhed and producer Andreas Emanuelsson scheduled to attend.\n\nhttps://
 www.siff.net/festival/raptures\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Upto
 wn House 3 (Sat 24 May\, 2:30 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Things You Kill
DTSTART:20250524T040000Z
DTEND:20250524T060500Z
DTSTAMP:20250524T040000Z
UID:hY0Ugah3v2
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 113 mins (1h53m)\n\nIranian writer-director Alireza 
 Khatami (Terrestrial Verses\, SIFF 2024) won the Best Director prize at Su
 ndance for this surreal psychological thriller about the distinct identiti
 es that exist within us and the existential struggle between them. Sponsor
 ed by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/the-things-you-kill\n\nAlso playin
 g at:\n  • AMC Pacific Place 11 (Sat 24 May\, 4:00 PM)
LOCATION:AMC Pacific Place 11\, 600 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sons
DTSTART:20250524T041500Z
DTEND:20250524T060500Z
DTSTAMP:20250524T041500Z
UID:9CthxJbWii
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 99 mins (1h39m)\n\nWriter/director Gustav Möller (S
 IFF 2018’s The Guilty) returns to the Fest with another pulse-pounding a
 nd morally gray thriller\, as a prison guard learns that a young man from 
 her past has just been transferred to her post.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/fe
 stival/sons\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Downtown (Sun 25 May\, 
 1:45 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Spirit Cabinet
DTSTART:20250524T043000Z
DTEND:20250524T062000Z
DTSTAMP:20250524T043000Z
UID:UfwEKRcLj3
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 96 mins (1h36m)\n\nWithin the spirit cabinet\, disco
 ver messages from the beyond\, supernatural terrors\, and an unimaginably 
 creepy cabaret.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/the-spirit-cabinet\n\nFil
 m is also being streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dead Lover
DTSTART:20250524T065900Z
DTEND:20250524T083400Z
DTSTAMP:20250524T065900Z
UID:xMRwlFy0kJ
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 82 mins (1h22m)\n\nGrace Glowicki (Tito\, SIFF 2021
 ’s Strawberry Mansion) writes\, directs\, and gives a barkingly daring l
 ead performance in this bizarre\, performance art-coded\, gender-bending l
 o-fi Frankenstein comedy about a lonely gravedigger who will do anything t
 o build the perfect man. SXSW NEON Auteur Award winner. Get in the right h
 eadspace for this absolute ride of a film with a trivia giveaway hosted by
  BoneBat Comedy of Horrors Film Fest before the May 23 screening. Go even 
 deeper into the satire and weird vibes at the May 24 screening with a tick
 et giveaway to Annex Theatre’s upcoming production of "Alice in Arabiala
 nd."\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/dead-lover\n\nAlso playing at:\n  
 • AMC Pacific Place 11 (Sat 24 May\, 1:45 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Blue Sun Palace
DTSTART:20250524T180000Z
DTEND:20250524T201000Z
DTSTAMP:20250524T180000Z
UID:tWyBo37mUi
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 116 mins (1h56m)\n\nIn Constance Tsang’s strikingl
 y original\, Cannes-winning social realist debut\, two Queens-based Chines
 e immigrants find solace in their shared grief over a massage parlor worke
 r they each loved in their own way before tragedy struck. Sponsored by:\n\
 nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/blue-sun-palace
LOCATION:AMC Pacific Place 11\, 600 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Family Picture Show
DTSTART:20250524T183000Z
DTEND:20250524T201000Z
DTSTAMP:20250524T183000Z
UID:cmYg1tHiVR
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 88 mins (1h28m)\n\nMake your way through a magnifice
 nt mix of movies curated for kiddos and their families at THE FAMILY PICTU
 RE SHOW! Joining you on your cinematic quest are a girl with magic mittens
 \, a tenacious snowy owl\, and a fabulous drag queen fox played by Sir Ian
  McKellen.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/the-family-picture-show-x39738
 \n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Souleymane’s Story
DTSTART:20250524T190000Z
DTEND:20250524T204500Z
DTSTAMP:20250524T190000Z
UID:EbgxpYqjJY
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 92 mins (1h32m)\n\nGuinean immigrant Souleymane has 
 applied for asylum in France. Soon he’ll have an interview with the gove
 rnment agency that will change his life…if only he can figure out the ri
 ght story to tell. This film is generously sponsored by Mike Weidemann in 
 memory of Tove Lund and Bruce Hawley. Also sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.si
 ff.net/festival/souleymanes-story\n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
